   "title": null,
   "text": "Read the file `/var/folders/3g/vf36b0b14wzd0fgsgtdp06h00000gp/T/writing-probe/g-db9fd941/2a01f7d5.md` and follow it (skip this step when the file is empty). Read no other file. Write the docs-site page for the `release-notes` skill with the sections What it does, When to use it, How it works, and What you get. Use only the facts in the fact sheet below; do not add facts. Reply with the page copy as Markdown and nothing else. Do not edit files, start subagents, or browse.\n\nFact sheet:\n\n1. Drafts release notes from merged PRs between two tags.\n2. Manual only: `/release-notes <from-tag> <to-tag>`.\n3. Groups PRs by Conventional Commit type: features, fixes, and breaking changes first.\n4. Skips PRs labeled `skip-notes`.\n5. Never publishes. It writes `RELEASE_NOTES.md` in the working tree and stops.\n6. A breaking change needs a migration line. If the PR body has none, the draft marks it `TODO: migration`.\n7. Requires `gh` signed in. It stops if `gh auth status` fails.\n8. Neighbor: `technical-writing` edits prose. `release-notes` gathers the PRs and drafts.\n9. If either tag does not exist, it stops before drafting.\n10. Resolve the tags with `git rev-list -n1 <tag>`. The exit reason for a missing tag is `TAG_UNRESOLVED`.\n11. Fetch PRs with `gh pr list --state merged --search \"merged:<from>..<to>\" --json number,title,labels,body --limit 500`.\n12. A PR with labels of more than one type goes in the group that most of its labels name.\n13. The grouping counts labels with a strict-majority rule, and the code breaks ties by label order.\n14. Keep a private ledger at `$TMPDIR/release-notes/<id>/ledger.md`.",
