   "text": "# release-notes\n\n## What it does\n\nDrafts release notes from merged PRs between two tags. `release-notes` gathers the PRs and drafts the notes; `technical-writing` edits prose.\n\n## When to use it\n\nUse it when you want a release-notes draft for a tag range. It runs only when invoked manually:\n\n```text\n/release-notes <from-tag> <to-tag>\n```\n\nBoth tags must exist, and `gh` must be signed in. The skill stops before drafting if either tag is missing or `gh auth status` fails.\n\n## How it works\n\nIt groups PRs by Conventional Commit type, with features, fixes, and breaking changes first. PRs labeled `skip-notes` are excluded.\n\nEach breaking change needs a migration line. If the PR body has none, the draft marks it `TODO: migration`.\n\n## What you get\n\nA `RELEASE_NOTES.md` file in the working tree. The skill writes the draft and stops. It never publishes.",
